synthesis
  The local star theorem is q-agnostic: primality is not used.
  Prime powers matter because they are p-adic tree branches, not because
  their local interval geometry is harder.
  A nonempty LRC endpoint core must mix descendant/off-grid/event labels;
  one zero branch cannot hold the core by itself.
